From: BrunoKlu <BrunoKlu@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] HT Capabilities element: 26 octets, bounded copies

struct rtw_ieee80211_ht_cap declared tx_BF_cap_info and
antenna_selection_info as __le16 each, so the element written in the
Association Request was 25 octets instead of 26. MediaTek access points
(MT7981) ACK such a request and never answer it. Use __le32 + u8 as in
802.11, and bound the copy of the AP's element in HT_caps_handler() to
the size of HT_cap[].

Added for OpenX6X00 (#29, #32): the other copies on the station's
receive path (beacons, probe responses, authentication and association
responses) that fill a fixed buffer for a length read from the frame,
bounded:
- rtw_check_bcn_info(), on every beacon with the associated AP's BSSID:
  the SSID, up to 255 octets, went into Ssid[32] and on over the rest of
  the WLAN_BSSID_EX, IELength included. Over 32 is now a mismatch, as a
  different SSID is (collect_bss_info() bounds it the same way).
- update_sta_support_rate() (IBSS): a peer's rates went into
  SupportedRates[16] and on into the next FW_sta_info entry. Refused now.
- WFD_info_handler(), for a vendor element with the WFD OUI in the
  Association Response (CONFIG_P2P and CONFIG_WFD are on): the element,
  up to 257 octets, went into wfd_ie[128] on the stack, and its Device
  Information attribute, up to 65535 octets, into attr_content[10]. An
  element over 128 octets, or an attribute under 4 or over 10, is now
  ignored.
- OnAuthClient(), shared key authentication: the challenge text, up to
  255 octets, went into chg_txt[128] and on through mlme_ext_info. The
  driver turns to shared key by itself when an AP answers status 13, so
  whoever answers a join gets there. Over 128 now fails the
  authentication.
- rtw_cfg80211_inform_bss(), for every scan result while a scan is
  pending: the WPS Selected Registrar attribute, up to 65535 octets, went
  into the one-octet sr on the stack. Now read only when it is one octet
  inside the element.
- rtw_get_wps_attr(), under the last one: the attribute length + 4 was a
  u16, so a length of 0xFFFC made a step of 0 and the walk never ended,
  with the scan queue's lock held. It is a u32 now.
Checked and left:
- Already bounded: collect_bss_info() (the elements, SSID, rates),
  join_cmd_hdl(), HT_info_handler(), bwmode_update_check(),
  ERP_IE_handler(), rtw_restructure_ht_ie() (the HT information element
  only at its exact size), and the frame rtw_cfg80211_inform_bss() builds
  (1000 octets).
- Reads past an element, inside the received buffer, and fixed-size
  copies: WMM_param_handler(), update_TSF(), the ADDBA request, the HT
  element fields read without a length check, rtw_get_wfd_attr_content()
  (up to 12 octets past wfd_ie[128]), and OnBeacon()'s
  CONFIG_ATTEMPT_TO_FIX_AP_BEACON_ERROR, which rewrites the Extended
  Supported Rates element's own length octet in the frame.
- Reads only, the helpers called without an output buffer:
  rtw_get_sec_ie() in rtw_get_bcn_info() and rtw_check_bcn_info(), and
  rtw_get_wps_ie(), rtw_get_p2p_ie() and rtw_get_wapi_ie() where they
  only find an element.
- Wi-Fi Direct only, reached once user space starts P2P (a scan for
  DIRECT- with a P2P element, remain-on-channel, a P2P GO), which nothing
  on the radio does: process_p2p_ps_ie() (the NoA attribute into
  noa_attr[256]), on_action_public_p2p() and the rtw_p2p.c frame handlers
  (attributes into small stack arrays), rtw_p2p_check_frames(), the
  listen channel of a probe request in collect_bss_info(), and
  rtw_get_p2p_attr(), whose length + 3 is a u16 as rtw_get_wps_attr()'s
  was.
- Wireless extensions only, ioctls nothing on the radio issues
  (NetworkManager and wpa_supplicant use nl80211; there are no
  wireless-tools): translate_scan()'s rtw_get_sec_ie() into
  wpa_ie[255] and rsn_ie[255] (a 255-octet element is 257 with its
  header) and its hex dump into 512 octets, its WFD filter, and the P2P
  private ioctls.
- AP mode only, which the radio never runs (the handlers return outside
  AP state): OnAuth(), OnAssocReq(), rtw_ap.c, the beacon and probe
  response builders.
- Compiled out: rtw_tdls.c (CONFIG_TDLS), the VHT handlers
  (CONFIG_80211AC_VHT), WAPI, Intel WiDi, CONFIG_ATMEL_RC_PATCH,
  CONFIG_AUTO_AP_MODE, CONFIG_DFS.
- Not audited here: element lists that user space sets through cfg80211
  (not frames), and the data path (A-MSDU, defragmentation, 802.11w),
  which parses no elements.
struct HT_caps_element stays as it is: HT_cap[26] makes its union 26
octets already; its struct view is not packed, and a __le32
Beamforming_caps there would make it 32.
---
diff --git a/core/rtw_ieee80211.c b/core/rtw_ieee80211.c
--- a/core/rtw_ieee80211.c
+++ b/core/rtw_ieee80211.c
@@ -993,7 +993,8 @@ u8 *rtw_get_wps_attr(u8 *wps_ie, uint wp
 		// 4 = 2(Attribute ID) + 2(Length)
 		u16 attr_id = RTW_GET_BE16(attr_ptr);
 		u16 attr_data_len = RTW_GET_BE16(attr_ptr + 2);
-		u16 attr_len = attr_data_len + 4;
+		// u32: in a u16, a length of 0xFFFC + 4 is a step of 0 and the walk never ends
+		u32 attr_len = attr_data_len + 4;
 
 		//DBG_871X("%s attr_ptr:%p, id:%u, length:%u\n", __FUNCTION__, attr_ptr, attr_id, attr_data_len);
 		if( attr_id == target_attr_id )
diff --git a/core/rtw_mlme_ext.c b/core/rtw_mlme_ext.c
--- a/core/rtw_mlme_ext.c
+++ b/core/rtw_mlme_ext.c
@@ -1652,6 +1652,13 @@ unsigned int OnAuthClient(_adapter *pada
 				goto authclnt_fail;
 			}
 
+			// the challenge text is 128 octets, its length the frame's
+			if (len > sizeof(pmlmeinfo->chg_txt))
+			{
+				DBG_871X("%s: challenge text too long (%u)\n", __FUNCTION__, len);
+				goto authclnt_fail;
+			}
+
 			_rtw_memcpy((void *)(pmlmeinfo->chg_txt), (void *)(p + 2), len);
 			pmlmeinfo->auth_seq = 3;
 			issue_auth(padapter, NULL, 0);
diff --git a/core/rtw_wlan_util.c b/core/rtw_wlan_util.c
--- a/core/rtw_wlan_util.c
+++ b/core/rtw_wlan_util.c
@@ -1233,11 +1233,20 @@ int WFD_info_handler(_adapter *padapter,
 	u32	wfd_ielen = 0;
 
 	pwdinfo = &padapter->wdinfo;
+	// the element's length is the AP's: rtw_get_wfd_ie() copies all of it
+	if (pIE->Length + 2 > sizeof(wfd_ie))
+		return _FAIL;
 	if (rtw_get_wfd_ie( ( u8* ) pIE, pIE->Length, wfd_ie, &wfd_ielen )) {
 		u8 attr_content[ 10 ] = { 0x00 };
 		u32 attr_contentlen = 0;
 
 		DBG_871X( "[%s] Found WFD IE\n", __FUNCTION__ );
+		// the attribute's length (16 bits) is the AP's too: ask for it first; the port is at +2
+		rtw_get_wfd_attr_content( wfd_ie, wfd_ielen,
+					  WFD_ATTR_DEVICE_INFO,
+					  NULL, &attr_contentlen);
+		if (attr_contentlen < 4 || attr_contentlen > sizeof(attr_content))
+			return _FAIL;
 		rtw_get_wfd_attr_content( wfd_ie, wfd_ielen,
 					  WFD_ATTR_DEVICE_INFO,
 					  attr_content, &attr_contentlen);
@@ -1578,7 +1587,7 @@ void HT_caps_handler(_adapter *padapter,
 
 	pmlmeinfo->HT_caps_enable = 1;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < (pIE->Length); i++)
+	for (i = 0; i < (pIE->Length) && i < sizeof(pmlmeinfo->HT_caps.u.HT_cap); i++)
 	{
 		if (i != 2)
 		{
@@ -1998,6 +2007,10 @@ int rtw_check_bcn_info(ADAPTER *Adapter,
 	}
 
 	if((NULL != p) && (_FALSE == hidden_ssid && (*(p + 1)))) {
+		if (len > NDIS_802_11_LENGTH_SSID) {
+			DBG_871X("%s(): SSID IE too long (%u)\n", __func__, len);
+			goto _mismatch;
+		}
 		_rtw_memcpy(bssid->Ssid.Ssid, (p + 2), *(p + 1));
 		bssid->Ssid.SsidLength = *(p + 1);
 	} else {
@@ -2832,12 +2845,21 @@ int update_sta_support_rate(_adapter *pa
 		return _FAIL;
 	}
 
+	if (ie_len > NDIS_802_11_LENGTH_RATES_EX)
+	{
+		return _FAIL;
+	}
+
 	_rtw_memcpy(pmlmeinfo->FW_sta_info[cam_idx].SupportedRates, pIE->data, ie_len);
 	supportRateNum = ie_len;
 
 	pIE = (PNDIS_802_11_VARIABLE_IEs)rtw_get_ie(pvar_ie, _EXT_SUPPORTEDRATES_IE_, &ie_len, var_ie_len);
 	if (pIE)
 	{
+		if (ie_len > (NDIS_802_11_LENGTH_RATES_EX - supportRateNum))
+		{
+			return _FAIL;
+		}
 		_rtw_memcpy((pmlmeinfo->FW_sta_info[cam_idx].SupportedRates + supportRateNum), pIE->data, ie_len);
 	}
 
diff --git a/include/wifi.h b/include/wifi.h
--- a/include/wifi.h
+++ b/include/wifi.h
@@ -710,8 +710,8 @@ struct rtw_ieee80211_ht_cap {
 	unsigned char	ampdu_params_info;
 	unsigned char	supp_mcs_set[16];
 	__le16	extended_ht_cap_info;
-	__le16		tx_BF_cap_info;
-	__le16	       antenna_selection_info;
+	__le32	tx_BF_cap_info;
+	unsigned char	antenna_selection_info;
 } __attribute__ ((packed));
 
 /**
diff --git a/os_dep/ioctl_cfg80211.c b/os_dep/ioctl_cfg80211.c
--- a/os_dep/ioctl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/os_dep/ioctl_cfg80211.c
@@ -428,11 +428,18 @@ struct cfg80211_bss *rtw_cfg80211_inform
 		struct cfg80211_ssid *ssids = request->ssids;
 		u32 wpsielen=0;
 		u8 *wpsie=NULL;
+		uint sr_len = 0;
 
 		wpsie = rtw_get_wps_ie(pnetwork->network.IEs+_FIXED_IE_LENGTH_, pnetwork->network.IELength-_FIXED_IE_LENGTH_, NULL, &wpsielen);
 
 		if(wpsie && wpsielen>0)
-			psr = rtw_get_wps_attr_content(wpsie,  wpsielen, WPS_ATTR_SELECTED_REGISTRAR, (u8*)(&sr), NULL);
+			psr = rtw_get_wps_attr_content(wpsie,  wpsielen, WPS_ATTR_SELECTED_REGISTRAR, NULL, &sr_len);
+
+		// Selected Registrar is one octet; the attribute's length is the AP's
+		if (psr && (sr_len != 1 || psr + 1 > wpsie + wpsielen))
+			psr = NULL;
+		if (psr)
+			sr = *psr;
 
 		if (sr != 0)
 		{
